==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Knight Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Pastry Cat''' when obtained from [[Samurai Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is very strong in [[Empire of Cats]]. Later in the game, his stats will be too low for him to have any use. His DPS is decent for his cost, but he will always die or get knocked back before any hit lands.

Even with these problems, he could still be seen as worthy to buy, as he is part of the [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] [[Cat Combo]], which provides a 15% attack boost to all units.

==='''True Form'''===
While Pastry Cat is able to slow non-Metal enemies, it is for only '''2 seconds''' with a '''10%''' chance. Coupled with Single Target and pathetic range, the only possible uses for his Slow are against [[Red Cyclone]], [[Dark Cyclone]], [[White Cyclone]] and [[Zyclone]], although nearly any [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] or [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]] alternative can outperform him.

==='''Talents'''===
Unlike most purchasable Special Cats, even Pastry Cat's [[Talents]] aren't enough to redeem him. His [[Barrier Breaker]] and [[Weaken]] are just as ineffective as his slow, as there are other Cats who are simply much better at providing these effects. Resist Slow is almost useless on a Cat like him. HP Buff doesn't improve his health enough to make him survive any decently strong attacks, while Attack Buff changes nothing when he can only land one or two hits at most.

==='''Orb'''===
Don't bother giving Pastry Cat an orb, as he is too expensive for his stats and abilities, making any Talent Orb useless.

