==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Knight Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]] called [[Valorous (Removed Combo)|Valorous]].
*Despite carrying a longer weapon, Samurai Cat has a shorter attack range compared to his other forms.
*The banner carried by Samurai Cat is a ''[[wikipedia:Sashimono|sashimono]]'', a banner carried by samurai warriors for easy identification.
*Knight Cat's evolution into Pastry Cat is explained by a pun in his Japanese descriptions: 菓子道 ''kashidō'' (way of the pastry) sounds almost like 騎士道 ''kishidō'' (way of the knight; chivalry). This pun is also shown in [[Chivalry and Candy (Combo)|Chivalry and Candy]].
*A character known as Samurai Cat appears in [[Battle Cats Quest]], though that Samurai Cat bears no resemblance beyond name to this Samurai Cat.
*In the Nintendo Switch port, Samurai Cat's true form goes unused, and given this case, when Zombies were added in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]], it was not granted Zombie targeting, making it and [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]] the only instances where a crowd-controller unit is unable to target a trait other than Metal or Traitless.
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Samurai Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Samurai Cat
Sincerity is the way of the warrior.
Exceptional health and attack.
A very well-rounded Cat.</pre>
<pre>Knight Cat
Added chivalry to his repertoire.
Exceptional health and attack.
A very well-rounded Cat.</pre>
<pre>Pastry Cat
Who says you can't love both cupcakes and
carnage? A kitchen pro who flings powerful
gobs of whipped cream to slow enemies.</pre>

